Well, finally had time to look at the source. From zap.c:

            if(rnd(20) < 18+u.uac) {
                register int dam = 0;
                range -= 2;
                pline("%s hits you!", The(fltxt));
                /* Checks for reflection and damage calctlations follow */
            } else pline("%s whizzes by you!", The(fltxt));

So at AC equal (or below) -18 the condition will always be false, and
any ray attacks will always 'whizz by you'.

Btw: searching zap.c I found and interesting piece of code:

        if(pl_character[0] == 'K' && type >= 10 && type <= 19 &&
           u.uhave.questart) tmp *= 2;

Which means, that if you are a knight carrying the magic mirror, then
any spell damage you do to the monsters is doubled!  Didn't know about
this extra effect of this 'most crappy quest artifact' as some want to
call it...
